## Why This Is Asked
Assess ability to design cost-aware routing in llm-ops, covering data modeling, routing decisions, isolation, and testability.

## Key Concepts
- Per-tenant budgeting and enforcement
- Usage tracking and token-cost calculation
- Request routing to model versions based on budget
- Data stores (Redis, Postgres) and caching strategies
- Testing: overage, latency, and drift

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code budget check before routing
if (budget.remaining <= 0) {
  return denyResponse();
}
if (budget.remaining < softLimit) {
  return degradeOrQueue();
}
routeTo(modelVersionBasedOnBudget());

```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle budget drift under bursty traffic?
- How would you test this under load with varying budgets and models?

